@startuml
participant "Alice main thread\n(login_cli loop)" as AM
participant "Alice reader\nlanlink-client-reader" as AR
participant "Server worker\nlanlink-‹id› (Alice)" as SW
participant "Bob reader\nlanlink-client-reader" as BR

note over AM
lanlink-cli-input reads "∕msg bob hi"
and puts it on the commands queue
end note
note over AM
send_private → _request:
_pending[request_id] = Queue(1)
end note
AM ->> SW : CHAT_PRIVATE (request_id,\nrecipient = bob, payload = "hi")
note over SW
_route_private:
bob in _users?
end note

alt bob online
  note over SW
  auth_ready.wait(1 s),
  recheck under _lock, stamp
  sender, message_id, timestamp_ms
  end note
  SW ->> BR : CHAT_PRIVATE (recipient,\nsender = alice, message_id,\ntimestamp_ms)
  note over BR
  display():
  "[alice -> bob] hi"
  end note
  SW ->> AR : CHAT_ACK (ref_request_id,\nmessage_id, timestamp_ms)
  AR ->> AM : reply put in queue\n_pending[ref_request_id]
  note over AM : print "Accepted: ‹message_id›"
else bob not in _users (offline or no such account)
  SW ->> AR : ERROR RECIPIENT_OFFLINE\n(ref_request_id)
  AR ->> AM : reply put in queue\n_pending[ref_request_id]
  note over AM
  _request raises LanLinkError,
  print "Request failed: ..."
  end note
else write to bob's socket raises OSError
  SW -[#C0392B]-> BR : _abort_connection:\nCLOSING, shutdown()
  SW ->> AR : ERROR CONNECTION_LOST\n(ref_request_id)
  AR ->> AM : reply put in queue\n_pending[ref_request_id]
  note over SW, BR
  Bob's worker sees CLOSING at its
  next wakeup (≤ WORKER_WAKEUP_S,
  0.5 s), exits, removes bob from _users
  end note
end
note over AM
read_next.set(): input thread
shows the next "> " prompt
end note

note over AM, BR
Public chat (∕all TEXT): CHAT_PUBLIC has no recipient.
_route_public sends it to every other online user, skips
(and aborts) a recipient whose write fails, then always
sends CHAT_ACK. CLI: "Accepted (best-effort broadcast)".
end note
@enduml
